  "hints": [
    {
      "tier": "direction",
      "text": "Start with the two requiresShipping methods \u2014 Product returns true, DigitalProduct overrides it to return false."
    },
    {
      "tier": "pattern",
      "text": "ShoppingCart.requiresShipping is an 'any match' loop: return true as soon as one product needs shipping, false after the loop."
    },
    {
      "tier": "key_insight",
      "text": "The strategies never check for DigitalProduct themselves. They ask the cart, and the cart asks each product \u2014 the override does the work through polymorphism."
    },
    {
      "tier": "pseudocode",
      "text": "requiresShipping: for item in lines: if item.product().requiresShipping() return true; return false. shippingCentsFor(a): return requiresShipping() ? Checkout.shippingCents(a) : 0. In strategies replace Checkout.shippingCents(x) with cart.shippingCentsFor(x)."
    }
  ],
